Purpose:
The gerp project takes in an input directory, and allows the user to search
for any word or series of words within that directory. All occurrences of 
that word, along with their file name and line numbers and the full line of
text, are printed to an output file. Searches can be case sensitive or case
insensitive. The program can be quit, and a new output file can be named
and created.

Acknowledgments:
I went to office hours with Daniel and Chris.
I received help, advice, and suggestions from Ariel Jacobs.

